  "raw_response": "def solve(grid):\n    rows, cols = len(grid), len(grid[0])\n    # Find the two non-zero cells\n    points = []\n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            if grid[r][c] != 0:\n                points.append((r, c, grid[r][c]))\n    \n    (r1, c1, v1), (r2, c2, v2) = points\n    \n    # Determine if pattern repeats along rows or columns\n    # Check if same column (horizontal lines) or same row (vertical lines)\n    if c1 == c2:\n        # Both in same column -> horizontal pattern\n        gap = r2 - r1\n        result = [row[:] for row in grid]\n        r = r1\n        i = 0\n        while r < rows:\n            for c in range(cols):\n                result[r][c] = v1 if i % 2 == 0 else v2\n            r += gap\n            i += 1\n        return result\n    elif r1 == r2:\n        # Both in same row -> vertical pattern\n        gap = c2 - c1\n        result = [row[:] for row in grid]\n        c = c1\n        i = 0\n        while c < cols:\n            for r in range(rows):\n                result[r][c] = v1 if i % 2 == 0 else v2\n            c += gap\n            i += 1\n        return result\n    else:\n        # Different row and column - check which axis to tile\n        dr = r2 - r1\n        dc = c2 - c1\n        result = [row[:] for row in grid]\n        \n        # Try column-based tiling (vertical stripes)\n        # Fill columns at c1, c2, c1+2*dc, etc.\n        c = c1\n        i = 0\n        while c < cols:\n            for r in range(rows):\n                result[r][c] = v1 if i % 2 == 0 else v2\n            c += dc\n            i += 1\n        \n        # Check if also row-based... look at examples 1&2: different rows, different cols\n        # In ex1: (0,5,2) and (9,7,8) - output has vertical stripes at cols 5,7,9,11...\n        # gap = 7-5=2, repeating with period 2 offsets\n        # Actually output: col 5=2, col 7=8, col 9=2, col 11=8... \n        # So it tiles columns with gap dc, alternating v1/v2\n        return result",
